CORE
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The expected sizes and offsets are those of x86-64 (LP64 and the x86-64
psABI); the source is guarded by __x86_64__, so the arm64 CI build runs it
vacuously (`-m64' is not accepted by the aarch64 gcc).  A 32-bit goto-cc
preprocesses with the 64-bit host gcc (__x86_64__ is defined) but lays out
for i386, so STATIC_ASSERT is vacuous unless sizeof(void *) is 8.
